The downstream impact is severe: at CR-composite layers, only the two 7--8B models show significant HS advantage; both 32B models fail. The CR-composite's systematic shallow-layer selection is an artifact of cosine compression (\cref{app:cosine_volatility}), not a genuine safety signal; random-label controls confirm this distinction (\cref{app:random_cp}). At threshold-based layers, the HS advantage is graded: cross-validated at 7--8B (OT-7B, R1-8B; nested CV), significant but suggestive of position-competitiveness at QwQ-32B$^\dagger$, and exploratory at R1-32B$^\dagger$ (residualized gap below MDE). The $\dagger$ marks sample-limited test sets ($n \leq 20$) where effect sizes are descriptive rather than confirmatory. Random-label controls on QwQ-32B and R1-8B confirm that threshold-based deep-layer selection requires genuine safety labels; the geometric shallow-layer bias is Qwen-specific: retained on QwQ-32B but dissolved on R1-8B (\cref{app:random_cp}). AUROC, excluded from our primary metrics because it is threshold-free (\cref{sec:evaluation}), confirms HS discriminability at BA-selected layers ($\Delta$AUROC +12.1 to +15.1pp; \cref{tab:ba_layer_results}) but cannot diagnose the threshold-dependent layer selection bias.\looseness=-1

\paragraph{Ensemble layer selection.} A three-layer ensemble that averages predicted probabilities from the precision-best, BA-best, and inverse-FPR-best layers bypasses single-metric pre-selection entirely. On the holdout split, all four models show significant HS advantage under the ensemble ($p \leq 0.002$, HB corrected; \cref{tab:ensemble}), including both 32B models that fail under CR-composite selection. The ensemble succeeds because averaging predictions from layers selected by different threshold-based metrics---which may favor somewhat different depths within the deep region---smooths metric-specific variation and reduces sensitivity to any single metric's layer preference. This holdout result uses the same split for both layer selection and evaluation; cross-validated confirmation is needed before the ensemble can be recommended as a general debiasing strategy (\cref{sec:discussion}).\looseness=-1

